/*
    `**` is the non-fusing product: its members are genuine two-tuples whose components
    are nested whole.
    Contrast with `*`, which fuses one level deep: `int * int * string` is a set of
    three-tuples regardless of grouping, while the members of `(int * int) ** string`
    are two-tuples whose first component is itself a two-tuple.
    `**` is what makes nesting expressible at all.
*/

(int * int) ** string
